From: XI14 <https://github.com/DavidFB-creator/MimOS>
Subject: [PATCH] users: give the credential fields an accessible name

The five fields a person must fill in to create their account expose an
accessible description and no accessible name. A screen reader leads with the
name, so a user tabbing into them hears an unnamed text field. Every other
interactive node on the reviewed pages is named.

Measured with AT-SPI against Calamares 3.4.2 under Wayland: 679 interactive
nodes across welcome, locale, keyboard, partition and users; five with no name;
none with neither a name nor a description. Keyboard navigation itself is fine,
so this is a labelling defect and not a navigation one.

The file carries no accessible* property at all and no <buddies> section, so Qt
has nothing to derive a name from. The description assistive technology does
see comes from placeholderText and toolTip. That is why the defect is easy to
miss: an audit that accepts "name or description" reports no problem here.

accessibleName is used rather than buddies because buddies would also change
what is announced for the labels themselves.

The strings are deliberately ones that ALREADY EXIST AND ARE TRANSLATED in this
file's own Qt context. A first version of this patch invented new source strings
-- "Full name", "Login name", "Computer name", "Repeat password" -- and they
announced in English on a Spanish system, because a new source string has no
translation in any of the sixty-odd catalogues Calamares ships. Only "Password"
came out right, and only by coincidence: it already existed here.

Qt resolves translations per context, so reusing a source string that is already
translated in Page_UserSetup fixes every language at once rather than only the
one someone thinks to check. "Repeat Password" versus "Repeat password" is a
single capital letter and it is the whole difference between "Repite la
contraseña" and English.

The full-name and computer-name fields therefore take their placeholder strings,
which does make the accessible name and description identical. That is a real
cost and it is smaller than announcing English. The login field takes its visible
question, which is verbose for an accessible name and correct in every language.

The two administrator fields keep new English strings: no suitable short label
exists translated in this context, and giving them the same names as the user
fields would put two identically named password fields on one page, which is
worse than untranslated. MimOS hides them, so nothing here reaches its users.

The two root-password fields are included: MimOS hides them, so they were not
in the measurement, but they are the same widgets with the same omission.

Reported upstream by MimOS (XI14). See docs/upstream/ in that project for the
measurement and the two instruments that gave wrong answers first.
---
--- a/src/modules/users/page_usersetup.ui
+++ b/src/modules/users/page_usersetup.ui
@@ -45,6 +45,9 @@
     <layout class="QHBoxLayout" name="fullNameLayout">
      <item>
       <widget class="QLineEdit" name="textBoxFullName">
+       <property name="accessibleName">
+        <string>Your Full Name</string>
+       </property>
        <property name="minimumSize">
         <size>
          <width>200</width>
@@ -132,6 +135,9 @@
     <layout class="QHBoxLayout" name="usernameLayout">
      <item>
       <widget class="QLineEdit" name="textBoxLoginName">
+       <property name="accessibleName">
+        <string>What name do you want to use to log in?</string>
+       </property>
        <property name="sizePolicy">
         <sizepolicy hsizetype="Expanding" vsizetype="Fixed">
          <horstretch>0</horstretch>
@@ -231,6 +237,9 @@
     <layout class="QHBoxLayout" name="hostnameLayout">
      <item>
       <widget class="QLineEdit" name="textBoxHostname">
+       <property name="accessibleName">
+        <string>Computer Name</string>
+       </property>
        <property name="sizePolicy">
         <sizepolicy hsizetype="Expanding" vsizetype="Fixed">
          <horstretch>0</horstretch>
@@ -333,6 +342,9 @@
     <layout class="QHBoxLayout" name="userPasswordLayout">
      <item>
       <widget class="QLineEdit" name="textBoxUserPassword">
+       <property name="accessibleName">
+        <string>Password</string>
+       </property>
        <property name="sizePolicy">
         <sizepolicy hsizetype="Expanding" vsizetype="Fixed">
          <horstretch>0</horstretch>
@@ -358,6 +370,9 @@
      </item>
      <item>
       <widget class="QLineEdit" name="textBoxUserVerifiedPassword">
+       <property name="accessibleName">
+        <string>Repeat Password</string>
+       </property>
        <property name="sizePolicy">
         <sizepolicy hsizetype="Expanding" vsizetype="Fixed">
          <horstretch>0</horstretch>
@@ -503,6 +518,9 @@
     <layout class="QHBoxLayout" name="rootPasswordLayout">
      <item>
       <widget class="QLineEdit" name="textBoxRootPassword">
+       <property name="accessibleName">
+        <string>Administrator password</string>
+       </property>
        <property name="sizePolicy">
         <sizepolicy hsizetype="Expanding" vsizetype="Fixed">
          <horstretch>0</horstretch>
@@ -528,6 +546,9 @@
      </item>
      <item>
       <widget class="QLineEdit" name="textBoxVerifiedRootPassword">
+       <property name="accessibleName">
+        <string>Repeat administrator password</string>
+       </property>
        <property name="sizePolicy">
         <sizepolicy hsizetype="Expanding" vsizetype="Fixed">
          <horstretch>0</horstretch>
